      en: "CGC Glass Works is a glass manufacturing plant in Bridgetown, Barbados, founded in 1965. It is the only producer of glass bottles on the island, producing over 100 million bottles annually for the beverage and food industries. The factory uses about 40% recycled glass and modern furnaces. It employs around 300 people, making it a key employer. The plant supplies local rum distilleries and breweries. Proximity to the port facilitates exports to the Caribbean. CGC Glass Works contributes to sustainability by recycling glass waste.",
